    "id": "3819506219",
    "isSimulated": false,
    "title": "TERMINAL 07",
    "description": "TERMINAL 07 is a minimal, monochrome system HUD.\n\nIt's based on [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3639973107]TERMINAL 02[/url] by sheet4.vn, restyled with a darker \"Void HUD\" look and extended with thermal monitoring and a live cooling schematic.\n\n[b]New in TERMINAL 07[/b]\n[list]\n[*] Void HUD theme: black background, cool-white text, soft bloom, no noise or scanlines\n[*] THERMAL panel: 2-minute CPU / GPU temperature and fan traces, session high / low, and headroom to the throttle point\n[*] Cooling schematic: fans spin at their real RPM, and heat pipes brighten and flow faster as the chips heat up\n[*] CPU / GPU temperature and fan speed columns in the performance monitor\n[*] Wind speed unit option (mph, km/h, m/s)\n[/list]\n\n[b]From TERMINAL 02[/b]\n[list]\n[*] Clock and date with minute / hour / day / week / month / year progress bars\n[*] Sunrise, sunset and weather from your latitude and longitude (suncalc + Open-Meteo)\n[*] Two world clocks\n[*] Now-playing music info and media history\n[*] System log\n[*] Hidden stopwatch: click the time box (double-click to exit)\n[*] Adjustable fonts, font size, margins, opacity, colors and filters\n[/list]\n\n[b]Setup[/b]\n[list]\n[*] Set your latitude, longitude and world clock time zones in the wallpaper properties.\n[*] The performance monitor, THERMAL panel and cooling schematic read from sheet4.vn's [url=https://github.com/sheetau/PerformanceMonitor/releases/latest]PerformanceMonitor[/url], which must be running.\n[*] CPU temperature and fan speeds need [url=https://www.hwinfo.com/]HWiNFO[/url] with \"Report value in Gadget\" turned on for those sensors. The included performance.layout.js is set up for an ASUS ROG Zephyrus G16 laptop. To adapt it, open the wallpaper folder, edit thermalConfig() to match your sensor names and throttle temperatures, and save it as performance.layout.user.js so updates don't overwrite it.\n[/list]\n\nIf the wallpaper affects your PC's performance, turn off bloom and the cooling schematic.\n\n[b]Credits[/b]\nThe original wallpaper, PerformanceMonitor and most of the code are by sheet4.vn. If you like this, check out the original [url=https://steamcommunity.com/sharedfiles/filedetails/?id=3639973107]TERMINAL 02[/url].",
